  "declarations": {
    "decision_A_icc_construction_axis": {
      "question": "p_11's PRIMARY axis is {truth, link}; BMMC's ladder has no link arm.",
      "declared_before_any_result": true,
      "primary": [
        "truth",
        "rand_celltype_x_donor_1to1"
      ],
      "reason": "within the pre-registered four-arm ladder this is the best-informed CONSTRUCTIBLE pairing -- cell-type labels and donor identity are both known at pairing time -- so it occupies link's role as 'what you use when you do not have truth'. rand_celltype_1to1 is the same construction with that knowledge deliberately discarded (a degraded variant, not the default choice); rand_global carries no cell-type signal and is excluded from every ICC axis, as PBMC excluded it, and is shown separately as floor_check so the exclusion is visible.",
      "also_reported": {
        "donor_contrast": [
          "truth",
          "rand_celltype_1to1",
          "rand_celltype_x_donor_1to1"
        ],
        "primary_link_nonladder": [
          "truth",
          "link"
        ],
        "sensitivity_ladder": [
          "truth",
          "rand_celltype_x_donor_1to1",
          "rand_celltype_1to1",
          "link_1to1",
          "link"
        ],
        "floor_check": [
          "truth",
          "rand_global"
        ]
      },
      "link_arms_are_scoreable_note": "link and link_1to1 were built for BMMC (prep_04_link.py, out/b04_link_report.json) but never carried into the GRN half. Track A needs only an assignment table, so they are scoreable here; both cover all 69,249 ATAC cells with zero barcodes absent from truth's matrix. Flagged ladder=false wherever they appear."
    },
    "decision_B_ksweep_k_list": {
      "question": "p_10's k-list and k=26 bar were described as PBMC-specific.",
      "declared_before_any_result": true,
      "k_list": [
        1,
        2,
        5,
        10,
        26,
        50
      ],
      "bar_k": 26,
      "bar": {
        "STRONG": ">= 0.50",
        "WEAK": "0.30 - 0.50",
        "NOT_RESCUED": "< 0.30"
      },
      "verdict": "L7 IS PORTED; the PBMC k-list and bar are carried over UNCHANGED.",
      "reason": "PIVOT_PREREGISTRATION.md \u00a78b defines the bar at 'k = 26 (the size of the T4 module the AML arm used)'. 26 is an AML-project constant -- the T4 module is 26 regulons / 14 TFs -- not a PBMC-derived one, so SCORING_RUNBOOK.md \u00a74 item 4 is wrong to call it PBMC-specific. Re-deriving a different k would destroy the only comparison the bar exists to support. Retention is checked against BMMC's own structure: BMMC's truth vocabulary is 221 Gene_based eRegulons (measured), so every k is drawable without replacement and the top rung is 50/221 = 22.6% of the vocabulary against PBMC's 50/245 = 20.4%. k=1 is not a free choice either: it is p_10's built-in consistency anchor against L6."
    },
    "declared_deviation_shared_draws": "b_08 generates each module draw-set ONCE per k and scores every arm on the identical modules, where p_10 consumed one running RNG and gave each arm different modules. The BMMC headline contrast is a one-variable arm pair; scoring the two arms on different random modules would confound the arm difference with a draw difference. No estimator changes.",
    "not_ported": "PIVOT_PREREGISTRATION.md \u00a78 L6's third variant -- activity residualised on cell-type one-hot + 5 diffusion components -- is not computed. PBMC's committed p_08 never computed it either, so there is no counterpart to compare against. Outstanding."
  },
